WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.780 --> 00:00:04.830
If 2020 was anything, it was a worldwide slap
in the face.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.468
Still, you'd think that some people would
be used to that sort of thing by now.

00:00:08.468 --> 00:00:13.049
The cast of "Jackass," for example, has made
a pretty solid living getting slapped in all

00:00:13.049 --> 00:00:14.400
sorts of places.

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:18.490
For most of us, 2020 made a simple trip to
the grocery store feel like a death-defying

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.430
stunt worthy of Knoxville and his pain-loving
cohort.

00:00:21.430 --> 00:00:26.240
If anyone was going to show up to the last
18 months with a subtle air of experience

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:31.872
and the collectively callused sense of dignity
necessary to keep soldiering on, it would have been them.

00:00:31.872 --> 00:00:32.644
Right?

00:00:32.644 --> 00:00:33.434
Kind of.

00:00:33.434 --> 00:00:38.199
In a recent interview with The Nine Club,
Jason "Wee Man" Acuña got candid about the

00:00:38.199 --> 00:00:43.320
process of creating the latest, and theoretically
final, installment of a story on par with

00:00:43.320 --> 00:00:46.537
the Marvel Cinematic Universe or The Skywalker
Saga.

00:00:46.537 --> 00:00:49.901
We are speaking, of course, of the "Jackass"
epic.

00:00:49.901 --> 00:00:55.510
"Jackass Forever" famously suffered from its
share of production setbacks due to interpersonal

00:00:55.510 --> 00:01:00.998
drama, but the COVID-19 pandemic proved to
be a predictably immense thorn in the movie's side.

00:01:00.998 --> 00:01:05.140
It turns out that making a movie about a bunch
of guys traveling and messing with strangers

00:01:05.140 --> 00:01:10.220
gets a little more difficult when said guys
can't travel or be around other people.

00:01:10.220 --> 00:01:14.702
Speaking on the subject of "Jackass Forever"
and the general "Jackass" body of work, The

00:01:14.702 --> 00:01:19.659
Nine Club host Chris Roberts expressed his
admiration for the cast's relaxed attitude

00:01:19.659 --> 00:01:21.680
with regards to mortal peril.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:25.450
That includes, of course, playing tetherball
with a hive of killer bees.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:30.990
Or pulling a real-life Fonz and attempting
an ill-fated leap over a family of circling sharks.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:35.969
Acuña was quick to point out that "Jackass
4" was shot with a different energy, and for

00:01:35.969 --> 00:01:38.912
that he blames - or credits - the global pandemic.

00:01:38.912 --> 00:01:39.912
He said,

00:01:39.912 --> 00:01:44.320
"This next one, because of COVID ... we couldn't
fly and mess with people and all that.

00:01:44.320 --> 00:01:47.259
I'll just say this: it's backyard 'f--k each
other up' stuff.

00:01:47.259 --> 00:01:48.439
That's all it is.

00:01:48.439 --> 00:01:50.222
And that's all I can say about it."

00:01:50.222 --> 00:01:55.079
Faced with that ominous teaser, Roberts became
concerned that a "different energy" might

00:01:55.079 --> 00:01:58.797
connote a lack of serious injuries sustained
by the cast.

00:01:58.797 --> 00:02:03.280
What would a fourth "Jackass" feature be without
the attendant emergency room visits and the

00:02:03.280 --> 00:02:06.260
ensuing barrage of insurance claims, after
all?

00:02:06.260 --> 00:02:11.340
Rest assured, Wee Man confirmed that he absolutely
hurt himself filming "Forever."

00:02:11.340 --> 00:02:16.090
Roberts didn't even finish asking "did you
ever get badly hurt?" before Acuña kicked

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.379
in, emphatically repeating the word "yes."

00:02:18.379 --> 00:02:23.140
He even went so far as to promise that, compared
to previous outings with the "Jackass" crew,

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:24.899
"this one hurt more."

00:02:24.899 --> 00:02:28.567
If that's not a guaranteed good time at the
theater, nothing is.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:33.461
"Jackass Forever" became part of the most
ill-timed class of productions in film history,

00:02:33.461 --> 00:02:38.495
as the crew attempted to begin shooting in
the halcyon days of the first quarter of 2020.

00:02:38.495 --> 00:02:43.140
At this time, the pandemic was in its infancy,
and very few people were even taking the early

00:02:43.140 --> 00:02:47.282
reports of a novel coronavirus in escalating
circulation seriously.

00:02:47.282 --> 00:02:51.970
As we all remember, that changed quickly,
and films in the midst of photography like

00:02:51.970 --> 00:02:55.310
"Jackass Forever" had to respond with due
haste.

00:02:55.310 --> 00:03:00.563
Many shut down completely, but to hear Wee
Man tell it, "Jackass Forever" took a different approach.

00:03:00.563 --> 00:03:01.629
Acuña said,

00:03:01.629 --> 00:03:06.069
"We started before COVID, we took the COVID
break, and Paramount used us as the guinea

00:03:06.069 --> 00:03:08.939
pig to see how studios could get back into
filming.

00:03:08.939 --> 00:03:11.505
And we had to do all the tests, and do it
all.

00:03:11.505 --> 00:03:13.620
And they're like, 'Well, 'Jackass' guys did
it.'

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.500
It was then used as a tool to get the other
ones going."

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:20.720
From how Acuña tells it, it sounds like Paramount
was more than willing to let the "Jackass"

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.590
crew serve as a proof of concept, putting
the cast's taste for danger up to viral scrutiny

00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:31.739
to see if a production could carry on under
a regime of rigorous testing and social distancing.

00:03:31.739 --> 00:03:36.269
Acuña went on to say the original goal was
to make "Jackass" fun again, which he attributes

00:03:36.269 --> 00:03:38.443
to the cast's now-advanced age.

00:03:38.443 --> 00:03:43.450
As luck would have it for fans of self-inflicted
pain, the pandemic busted up that vision for

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:44.539
whatever reason.

00:03:44.539 --> 00:03:46.390
"Okay, let's make it fun!

00:03:46.723 --> 00:03:52.380
But no, Covid made it--made us, COVID made
us beat each other up again."

00:03:52.380 --> 00:03:53.849
And why wouldn't it?

00:03:53.849 --> 00:03:58.969
"Jackass Forever" is slated to hit theaters
on October 22, 2021.

